ers/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T04:44:26Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T04:44:26Z","body":"No worries! 😄 It's happened to me a few times too, that I've written proposals, issues, or PRs only to find out there was a similar one buried in the repository somewhere.\r\n\r\nIt sounds to me like the one I did was more minimal (didn't have a `user_defined_project_path` or similar), otherwise I think they're pretty similar. What was the reasoning for the `user_defined_project_path` as opposed to reusing the existing `default_project_path`? Perhaps that would make your PR a better alternative?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3404504456/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3404510476","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111629#issuecomment-3404510476","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111629","id":3404510476,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7K7LUM","user":{"login":"Cautami","id":219921783,"node_id":"U_kgDODRu9dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219921783?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami","html_url":"https://github.com/Cautami","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T04:48:20Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T04:48:51Z","body":"I decided to create user_defined because I wanted to keep Godot's default path always accessible, mostly for the placeholder text if the user were to erase the path, or for a reset button to help encourage experimentation like a lot of Godot's properties enable. \r\nI was also partially worried overriding the behavior would have negative consequences if something out there relied on it, for whatever reason. Didn't want to stomp on anyone's toes. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3404510476/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]